ttychatter.mailbot 0.2.0
=========================

ttychatter.mailbot is a conservative IMAP/sendmail transport adapter for
ttychatter. It watches unread mail for subjects like tc:{session}, passes the
message body and attachments to ttychatter, and replies by email.

Version 0.2.0 fixes the important unread-mail bug from 0.1.0. The bot now uses
IMAP BODY.PEEK[] for inspection so dry-run and skipped messages do not become
read merely because the bot looked at them.

Files
-----

    ttychatter.mailbot
    ttychatter.mailbot.1
    ttychatter.mailbot.changelog
    MAILBOT-WALKTHROUGH

Typical commands
----------------

    ttychatter.mailbot --doctor
    ttychatter.mailbot --list-candidates
    ttychatter.mailbot --once --dry-run
    ttychatter.mailbot --once

Config-over-email
-----------------

Send an allowed message with:

    tc:{CONFIG}

No attachment means: send me the current config as an attachment.

An edited text config attachment means: replace the current config after making
a timestamped backup. Dry-run never writes config.

Security
--------

Set ALLOWED_FROM. Keep it narrow. Do not run a mailbot that accepts arbitrary
senders unless you want strangers spending your API quota.
